# Laravel Development Rules for Contractly

## General

- Use PHP 8.3+ features: constructor property promotion, readonly properties, enums, match expressions, named arguments
- Always use `declare(strict_types=1)` at the top of PHP files
- Follow PSR-12 coding standards
- Use Pint for code formatting
- Create Pest tests for all new features
- Avoid generating obvious code comments

## Architecture

### Controllers
- Keep controllers slim - delegate logic to Service classes
- Use single-action controllers with `__invoke()` for single-purpose endpoints
- Use Form Requests for validation, never validate in controllers
- Always return API Resources, never raw models

```php
// Good
class UploadContractController extends Controller
{
    public function __invoke(
        StoreContractRequest $request,
        ContractUploadService $service
    ): JsonResponse {
        $contract = $service->upload($request->validated());
        return ContractResource::make($contract);
    }
}
```

### Services
- Inject services directly into controller methods if used only once
- Initialize services in constructor if used across multiple methods
- Services contain business logic, controllers handle HTTP concerns

### Models
- Place Enums in `app/Enums` directory
- Cast columns to Enum types in models
- Register Observers using PHP Attributes on Models
- Update `$fillable` arrays when adding migration columns

```php
#[ObservedBy(ContractObserver::class)]
class Contract extends Model
{
    protected $casts = [
        'status' => ContractStatus::class,
    ];
}
```

## Facades over Helpers

Use full Facade imports instead of helper functions:

```php
// Good
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Auth;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Cache;

$userId = Auth::id();
$data = Cache::get('key');

// Avoid
$userId = auth()->id();
$data = cache('key');
```

## Code Patterns

### Use match over switch
```php
$label = match($status) {
    ContractStatus::PENDING => 'Waiting',
    ContractStatus::PROCESSING => 'Analyzing',
    ContractStatus::COMPLETED => 'Done',
};
```

### Eliminate temporary single-use variables
```php
// Good
return ContractResource::make($this->service->analyze($contract));

// Avoid
$result = $this->service->analyze($contract);
return ContractResource::make($result);
```

### Use Enums for fixed values
```php
enum ContractStatus: string
{
    case PENDING = 'pending';
    case PROCESSING = 'processing';
    case COMPLETED = 'completed';
}
```

## Database

- Run migration commands one at a time, no chaining with `&&`
- Always define foreign key constraints
- Use UUIDs for public-facing IDs
- Index columns used in WHERE clauses

## Testing

- Use Pest syntax
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
- Use factories for test data
- Mock external services (Claude API)

```php
it('uploads a contract successfully', function () {
    $user = User::factory()->create();
    $file = UploadedFile::fake()->create('contract.pdf');

    $response = $this->actingAs($user)
        ->postJson('/api/contracts', ['file' => $file]);

    $response->assertCreated();
});
```
